<title>USA: CME feeder cattle futures soar to 40-month high.</title>
<headline>CME feeder cattle futures soar to 40-month high.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-07-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>CME August feeder cattle futures rose sharply in early trade, posting the highest price in over three years, boosted by growing concerns about a shortage of supplies this fall.</p>
<p>Dealers said overnight losses in CBOT corn were also supportive.</p>
<p>August rose to a peak of 82.300 cents per lb, up 1.475 cent, a contract high and the strongest level for the nearby month since March 1994.</p>
<p>((Nigel Hunt 312-408 8720))</p>
</text>
